        {
          "id": 1080343159,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "`case col_link_` will need to be excluded from double click.  \n  \n[4.9. Link-layer header type](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html/#ChCapLinkLayerHeader):  \n> In most cases you won’t have to modify link-layer header type. Some exceptions are as follows:\n\n> If you are capturing on an Ethernet device you might be offered a choice of “Ethernet” or “DOCSIS”. If you are capturing traffic from a Cisco Cable Modem Termination System that is putting DOCSIS traffic onto the Ethernet to be captured, select “DOCSIS”, otherwise select “Ethernet”.\n\n> ...\n  \n(I went back to 3.6.7 and did some testing to compare to this commit.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
