        {
          "id": 1084412619,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "`case col_extcap_:` is not working with double-click. From what I read in the `Qt` forums, you always get a single-click signal/event before a double-click signal/event and need a timer to wait to see if a double-click is coming in.  \n  \nWith sound on, there is a \"dong\" when double clicking and the extcap options popup flashes. The same behavior can be seen on the Welcome page if you single click on the gear, wait for the popup then single click the gear again.   \n\nI was not able to ever double-click and get the extcap options to come up with the [\"Start\"](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/ui/qt/extcap_options_dialog.cpp#L72) button.  \n  \nShould double-click capture start be excluded for the \"gear\" column on Capture Options and Welcome page?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-08-31T19:47:19.988Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-08-31T19:47:19.988Z",
